WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.585 --> 00:00:10.275
I'm Kimberley Harvey.
I'm a dance artist, choreographer and teacher.

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:13.917
I have my own company, Subtle Kraft Co.,

00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:21.157
I'm a freelance artist and I also work for
Candoco Dance Company as a Candoco artist.

00:00:25.287 --> 00:00:30.180
For all of the work that I do,
whether as a choreographer or as a teacher,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.202
one of the key things for me
is always the relationship,

00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:38.108
whether to the space, to other people
or to myself.

00:00:38.108 --> 00:00:41.240
So, that runs through everything,
and then, on the top of that,

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.793
 over the past couple of years,
I've been gathering research

00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:48.278
around the use of holding

00:00:48.278 --> 00:00:52.043
based on my own and also with other artists.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.247
And so this idea of holding spaces
in different ways,

00:00:58.247 --> 00:01:02.868
and I'm drawn to spaces that hold me,

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:09.525
so, I will often choose to put myself
in corners

00:01:09.525 --> 00:01:13.442
or behind pillars or in alcoves

00:01:13.442 --> 00:01:16.257
where there is a kind of

00:01:16.257 --> 00:01:19.557
a sense of being held by the space.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:26.512
I have two works 
that really stand out for me.

00:01:26.512 --> 00:01:30.315
One is a solo that I made most recently

00:01:30.315 --> 00:01:32.957
called "Inky Matter"

00:01:32.957 --> 00:01:39.425
and where basically I'm fascinated by letters,
particularly handwritten ones,

00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:43.205
and for ages I thought that it was only me.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:52.080
And then I realised that I had lots of letters
in me that I've never written or that I've never sent,

00:01:52.515 --> 00:01:57.467
and then the more I talked to people,
the more I realised that they did as well.

00:01:59.393 --> 00:02:06.212
And also, for me, I placed the letters
in very particular parts of my body,

00:02:06.212 --> 00:02:11.197
so that, as a dancer,
was a perfect starting point.

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:19.843
And then the other one is a film
I made a few years ago,

00:02:22.758 --> 00:02:24.970
which is called "On the Tip of my Tongue",

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:29.515
which I made with a friend
and a colleague of mine,

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:35.438
and the reason I love it
is because it came from me

00:02:35.438 --> 00:02:41.077
going to Andrew Graham,
who is the other performer,

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:44.143
and saying:
"We've known each other for years

00:02:44.143 --> 00:02:48.482
but I've never actually directed with you.
I love what you do as a dancer

00:02:48.482 --> 00:02:53.587
and as an artist. I want to work
with you and I want to make a dance film."

00:02:53.587 --> 00:02:57.993
And I said "Would you be up for it?"
and he said “Yes”.

00:02:57.993 --> 00:03:04.580
And from there we then created the brief
of the film together.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.705
And it was what is our language
as a duet,

00:03:09.705 --> 00:03:13.852
because he is almost 6 foot
(183cm)

00:03:13.852 --> 00:03:17.593
and I'm definitely not 6 foot,

00:03:17.593 --> 00:03:21.982
and I'm out of the chair for part of it as well,

00:03:21.982 --> 00:03:25.633
so we did some in the chair
and some out of the chair,

00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:28.242
and because of the relationship
that we have,

00:03:28.242 --> 00:03:32.008
it's also one of trust,
I was able to do things with him

00:03:32.008 --> 00:03:33.792
in a very short space of time.

00:03:36.802 --> 00:03:41.198
I love that my job enables me

00:03:41.198 --> 00:03:45.400
to play and to communicate

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.590
in a variety of ways, as a teacher,
as a choreographer and as a performer.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.725
And I think as adults particularly,

00:03:52.725 --> 00:03:56.862
we lose the ability to play.
We get told that we are too old to play

00:03:56.862 --> 00:03:59.947
or that we should be serious now
because we are adults.

00:03:59.947 --> 00:04:04.107
In the dance environment you see
a micro world

00:04:04.107 --> 00:04:08.398
which is really beautiful and things
happen and are being made

00:04:08.398 --> 00:04:10.158
in a creative setting

00:04:10.158 --> 00:04:13.350
that you kind of wish you could
diffuse to everybody,

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.868
because we are not frightened of proximity,
we are less fearful of touch

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:23.022
and we are less fearful of communicating

00:04:23.022 --> 00:04:27.073
in a variety of diverse ways.

00:04:27.073 --> 00:04:31.397
There's an openness in the creative space
which there isn't in the wider world.

